      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an intelligent email assistant.\n\nAnalyze the following email and determine whether it contains a meeting invitation.\n\nEmail Subject:\n{{ $json.subject }}\n\nEmail Body:\n{{ $json.snippet }}\n\nIf the email contains a meeting, extract the following information.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this exact format:\n\n{\n  \"title\": \"Meeting Title\",\n  \"startDateTime\": \"2026-07-12T15:00:00+05:30\",\n  \"endDateTime\": \"2026-07-12T16:00:00+05:30\",\n  \"timezone\": \"Asia/Kolkata\",\n  \"meetingLink\": \"https://meet.google.com/abc-xyz\",\n  \"summary\": \"Short description of the meeting\",\n  \"participants\": [\n    \"Participant 1\",\n    \"Participant 2\"\n  ],\n  \"organizer\": \"Organizer Name\",\n  \"isMeeting\": true\n}\n\nInstructions:\n- Read the email carefully.\n- If a meeting date and time are mentioned, convert them into ISO 8601 format.\n- If the email uses IST, convert it to Asia/Kolkata (+05:30).\n- Set endDateTime to one hour after startDateTime unless another duration is specified.\n- Extract the Google Meet, Zoom, Teams or any meeting link if available.\n- Extract all participant names if mentioned.\n- Extract the organizer name if available.\n- Generate a short summary of the meeting.\n- Set \"isMeeting\" to true only if the email is actually about a meeting; otherwise set it to false.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON.\n- Do not include markdown, explanations, or any extra text.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
